#. type: Title =
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Picking the Army"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:7
msgid ""
"This section of the Warmaster Armies book explains how to choose equally "
"matched armies to take part in a battle and updates the original section in "
"the main rulebook."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:13
msgid ""
"In theory there is no reason why forces have to be equal, but most players "
"prefer to fight battles between armies that are, notionally at least, the "
"same fighting value. To facilitate this, all units are allocated a points "
"value that reflects their worth in a typical battle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:21
msgid ""
"As a matter of principle the points values of individual units are "
"considered in proportion to the army as a whole so that troops of comparable "
"fighting value may be a few points more or a few points less in some armies. "
"This is intentional. In these cases the marginal difference in points is "
"done to restrict or increase the choices available to the player."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Army"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:31
msgid ""
"Army lists and rules are provided for 25 Warmaster armies. All armies are "
"chosen in the same fashion using the appropriate list. The army lists are "
"included on the following pages and you may wish to skip forward to your "
"favoured army as you read through the rest of this section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "Army size"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:40
msgid ""
"Both sides select troops and characters up to the same maximum points value. "
"Three ’standard’ sized battles are considered here. Smaller and larger "
"battles, or battles with intermediate points values, can also be arranged as "
"discussed later."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Small battle   |1000 points per side\n"
"|Medium battle  |2000 points per side\n"
"|Large battle   |3000 points per side\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:58
msgid ""
"A small battle is ideal for beginners or for demonstrating the game but the "
"tactical possibilities are limited. Small battles are more susceptible to "
"the fortunes of dice rolling than are large battles. Medium sized battles "
"are considered the usual kind and will typically last for a whole evening’s "
"play – although experienced players have been known to cram four or more "
"such battles into a single day."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:69
msgid ""
"Large battles require more leisure but offer a varied game that better "
"reflects the subtleties of the command system.  Substantially bigger battles "
"can be fought with even more points per side if players wish. Beware that a "
"very large game can take an entire day or even several days to complete. "
"There is no real maximum limit beyond the number of models and the size of "
"the gaming area available. 10,000 points or more is certainly feasible.  "
"With very large armies it helps to have additional players to help move "
"troops and roll dice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:78
msgid ""
"Note that the army size indicates the maximum points value that can be "
"spent. Armies can have fewer points than this value but cannot have more. "
"Often it is impossible to spend the odd few points so a medium sized ‘2000 "
"point’ army might have only 1995 points of models. Such an army is still a "
"2000 point army as far as we are concerned. It is the maximum permitted "
"value that determines the army size not the actual points spent."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:86
msgid ""
"The army lists are designed to work with armies of round thousands of points "
"(1000, 2000, 3000, etc). However, it is also possible to choose armies of "
"other sizes – say 1500 or 750.  This is slightly less convenient but useful "
"if players are still building their armies and want to use units as they are "
"purchased. This is explained under Selecting the Army."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "Army lists"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:98
msgid ""
"Begin with the army list for your chosen army. The different lists include "
"all the units available for each side together with their game stats, points "
"values and special rules where appropriate. Most of this information is "
"condensed into a single stat line for each unit. Any additional information "
"is noted as special rules after the army list itself. Stat lines are "
"presented as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:106
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Troop |Type |Attacks |Hits |Armour |Command |Unit size |Points |Min/max |Special\n"
"\n"
"|Halberdiers |Infantry |3 |3 |6+ |– |3 |45 |2/– |–\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:108
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/table-attributes.adoc:13
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:237
#, no-wrap
msgid "Type"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:113
msgid ""
"This describes the type of troop unit or character stand: Infantry, Cavalry, "
"Monster, Artillery, Machine, Chariot, General, Wizard or Hero. Mounts for "
"characters are sometimes optional and are included as a separate line as "
"Monstrous Mount or Chariot Mount."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:114
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:239
#, no-wrap
msgid "Attack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:116
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:240
msgid "The basic number of dice rolled in combat by each stand in the unit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:117
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/table-attributes.adoc:15
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:241
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hits"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:119
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:242
msgid "The number of hits the unit can suffer before one stand is removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:120
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/table-attributes.adoc:16
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/combat.adoc:410
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:243
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:250
#, no-wrap
msgid "Armour"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:123
msgid ""
"The score required to nullify a hit struck on the unit if it has armour (3+, "
"4+, 5+ or 6+). A unit with no armour has a value of 0."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:124
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/table-attributes.adoc:17
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-sequence.adoc:51
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:245
#, no-wrap
msgid "Command"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:125
msgid "The Command value of a character."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:126
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/table-attributes.adoc:18
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:247
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unit size"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:127
msgid "The number of stands in a unit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Attribute :points-per-unit:
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:128
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/table-attributes.adoc:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "Points per unit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:130
msgid "The points value of a unit or character of that type."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:131
#, no-wrap
msgid "Min/Max"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:135
msgid ""
"This defines the minimum and maximum number of units of that type which an "
"army must include per 1000 points of army size. A dash indicates there is no "
"restriction."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:137
#, no-wrap
msgid "Selecting the army"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:143
msgid ""
"Choose units and characters to make up the army. You can choose up to a "
"maximum total value appropriate to the size of game. For example, High Elf "
"Spearmen are 60 points per unit so 5 such units are worth 300 points."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:155
msgid ""
"Players are not entirely free to select forces as they want.  Some units "
"must always be included and some other units can only be included in limited "
"numbers. These restrictions are indicated by the minimum/maximum column (min/"
"max) in the army lists. The min/max value consists of two numbers separated "
"by a slash – for example 1/2. The first number shows the minimum number of "
"that unit/character the army must include for every 1000 points of army "
"size. The second number shows the maximum number of that unit/character the "
"army can include for every 1000 points of army size."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:162
msgid ""
"For example, in a Bretonnian army, Squires are min/max 1/4. This means that "
"in a 1000 point army the player must include at least 1 unit but cannot "
"include more than 4. In a 2000 point army the minimum is therefore 2 and the "
"maximum 8, in a 3000 point army minimum 3 maximum 12, and so on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:170
msgid ""
"If an entry includes a dash instead of a number this means no minimum or "
"maximum applies. The player can chose as few or as many of this troop types "
"as he wishes within the limitations of the points available. For example, "
"–/2 means that in a 1000 points army there is no minimum and the maximum is "
"2, while 1/– means there is a minimum of 1 and no maximum."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:180
msgid ""
"All armies must include a single General. An army can never include more "
"than one General no matter what its size. The Min/Max column is given as 1 "
"to show this.  You may have decided your armies will be chosen to 1500 "
"points or some other odd number. In this case determine min/max values by "
"rounding your actual army size down to the next full 1000’s. So, a 1500 "
"point army is selected using the minimums and maximums for a 1000 point "
"army, a 2250 point army is the same as a 2000 and so on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:187
msgid ""
"If your chosen army size is less than 1000 points then use the 1000 point "
"maximums but ignore the minimums.  Very small games can be a useful exercise "
"for learning the rules but be warned that the game does not work "
"particularly well with extremely small forces and battles may feel "
"bewilderingly rapid."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/picking-the-army.adoc:196
msgid ""
"The value of any permitted magic items is added to that of the unit or "
"character that carries them. Magic items must be allocated to specific "
"characters and a separate note made. This will increase the points value of "
"the unit or character appropriately, and the total cost must be taken into "
"account when working out victory points. See Magic in the rulebook p.76 or a "
"Magic Items Overview on p.88 in this book."
msgstr ""
